      viewing_task: "<ol><li><strong>[01:10] Recall:</strong> In what month and year was UN Security Council Resolution 242 unanimously adopted, and what was the name of the British UN ambassador who drafted its delicate text?</li><li><strong>[02:35] Explain:</strong> Explain the diplomatic architecture of the 'Land for Peace' formula created by Resolution 242.</li><li><strong>[03:50] Challenge:</strong> Analyze the crucial linguistic loophole between the English version ('withdrawal from territories occupied') and the French version ('retrait des territoires occupés'). Why did this linguistic ambiguity cause decades of diplomatic stalemate?</li></ol>",
